WEBVTT

00:00.387 --> 00:03.062
Use the page's invented one-week pilot.

00:03.062 --> 00:05.396
An engineer and reviewer must choose the meeting's

00:05.396 --> 00:08.635
measure and explain the report's older hundred percent.

00:08.635 --> 00:11.879
A database collector supplies table and view structure;

00:11.879 --> 00:14.897
job and report records still need manual updates.

00:14.897 --> 00:18.431
Would installing that collector establish the incident's explanation?

00:18.431 --> 00:20.944
Name what evidence is missing, then pause.

00:26.133 --> 00:31.189
The reviewer needs to trace the refresh to its output, run, retained input and code,

00:31.189 --> 00:33.203
then find the later failed run.

00:33.203 --> 00:36.671
A structural scan supplies none of that chain by itself.

00:36.671 --> 00:39.274
Test whether an independent reviewer can open the

00:39.274 --> 00:42.432
retained evidence, rather than merely see links.

00:42.432 --> 00:46.674
Exports must preserve source identifiers, times and version references.

00:47.683 --> 00:49.694
Now read the illustrative assessment.

00:49.694 --> 00:54.458
Both questions are answered, collection failure is visible, and access checks pass for

00:54.457 --> 00:56.141
tested accounts and paths.

00:56.141 --> 00:59.617
Maintenance takes ninety minutes a week, within a two-hour budget.

00:59.617 --> 01:03.164
Changes appear the same working day, within the one-day limit.

01:03.164 --> 01:07.364
What platform decision follows, and how far can that conclusion extend?

01:07.363 --> 01:08.284
Pause to explain.

01:13.167 --> 01:16.498
Keep reviewed documents and SQLite for those two questions.

01:16.498 --> 01:20.654
This is an invented teaching outcome, not an assessment of a catalogue product.

01:20.654 --> 01:24.856
Job and report updates remain manual; other sources are untested.

01:24.856 --> 01:25.811
Review weekly.

01:25.811 --> 01:30.051
Trial a catalogue if maintenance exceeds two hours a week or updates take longer than

01:30.051 --> 01:33.182
one working day, checking exact source and version support.

01:34.042 --> 01:35.813
Continuing work needs an owner.

01:35.813 --> 01:38.176
The reporting engineer handles collection failures

01:38.176 --> 01:41.347
and checks the last successful observation's age.

01:41.347 --> 01:44.729
Definition responsibility stays with the relevant business team.

01:44.729 --> 01:47.468
Protect metadata too: descriptions, queries

01:47.468 --> 01:49.965
or samples can reveal sensitive information.

01:49.965 --> 01:53.541
Repeat access checks when permissions or interfaces change.

01:53.541 --> 01:57.892
Collector upgrades also require checking identifiers, fields and evidence links.

01:59.060 --> 02:00.762
Try the page's map exercise.

02:00.762 --> 02:03.368
Open Collection run's Example record.

02:03.368 --> 02:08.600
Name one structural fact the scan supports and one missing kind of incident evidence.

02:08.600 --> 02:11.038
Then inspect Responsible team.

02:11.038 --> 02:15.284
Explain why installing a collector neither supplies complete incident coverage nor

02:15.284 --> 02:17.740
transfers definition ownership to its operator.

02:17.740 --> 02:19.461
Use Check your answer.

02:19.461 --> 02:22.392
The map does not measure pilot effort or assess a product.
